<table cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0>


	<tr>
		<td valign="top" class="headline8" colspan="2">Baghdad Is Hit by Arson and Looting; U.S. Troops Are Ordered to Stop the Plunder</td>
		<td valign="top" rowspan="3" width="95" class="imagecredit8"><a href="/news/data/8_ds_437627.asp"><img src="/dsdsmultimedia/photos/WAR_IRAQ_US_BAGHDAD9.jpg" width="85" border="0"></a></td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td valign="top" colspan="2" class="citation8">Looting surged and government buildings were set on fire across Baghdad on Thursday while U.S. troops concentrated more on fighting pockets of resistance than on keeping order.&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="/news/data/8_ds_437627.asp">Full Story</a>
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td valign="top" class="imagecredit8">AP Photo &#150; JEROME DELAY
		</td>
		<td valign="top" align="right" class="time8">&nbsp;
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td valign="top" colspan="3">&nbsp;
		</td>
	</tr>





	<tr>
		<td valign="top" class="headline8" colspan="2">Bush Speaks to Iraqi People in TV Address, Says 'Regime of Saddam Hussein Is Being Removed'</td>
		<td valign="top" rowspan="3" width="95" class="imagecredit8"><a href="/news/data/8_ds_437703.asp"><img src="/dsdsmultimedia/photos/IRAQ_WAR_KURDS_NORTH19.jpg" width="85" border="0"></a></td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td valign="top" colspan="2" class="citation8">President Bush, launching a massive media campaign in war-torn Iraq, said in a nationally televised address Thursday, "Your nation will soon be free." British ally Tony Blair assured Iraqis that coalition soldiers are "friends and liberators, not your conquerors."&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="/news/data/8_ds_437703.asp">Full Story</a>
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td valign="top" class="imagecredit8">AP Photo &#150; KAMRAN JEBREILI
		</td>
		<td valign="top" align="right" class="time8">&nbsp;
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td valign="top" colspan="3">&nbsp;
		</td>
	</tr>





	<tr>
		<td valign="top" class="headline8" colspan="2">Marines Battle Holdouts at Baghdad Palace, Mosque; America's Kurdish Allies Enter Key Oil City</td>
		<td valign="top" rowspan="3" width="95" class="imagecredit8"><a href="/news/data/8_ds_437638.asp"><img src="/dsdsmultimedia/photos/TOPIX_IRAQ_US_MILITA.jpg" width="85" border="0"></a></td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td valign="top" colspan="2" class="citation8">U.S. forces battled holdout fighters Thursday at a palace and a mosque in Baghdad; one Marine was killed and up to 20 wounded. In the north, America's Kurdish allies achieved a major breakthrough - entering the city of Kirkuk near some of Iraq's most productive oil fields.&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="/news/data/8_ds_437638.asp">Full Story</a>
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td valign="top" class="imagecredit8">AP Photo &#150; LAURA RAUCH
		</td>
		<td valign="top" align="right" class="time8">&nbsp;
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td valign="top" colspan="3">&nbsp;
		</td>
	</tr>





	<tr>
		<td valign="top" class="headline8" colspan="2">Kurdish Fighters Enter Strategic Oil City of Kirkuk in Northern Iraq</td>
		<td valign="top" rowspan="3" width="95" class="imagecredit8"><a href="/news/data/8_ds_437416.asp"><img src="/dsdsmultimedia/photos/IRAQ_WAR_US_NORTHERN23.jpg" width="85" border="0"></a></td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td valign="top" colspan="2" class="citation8">A convoy of Kurdish peshmerga fighters moved into the oil-rich city of Kirkuk on Thursday.&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="/news/data/8_ds_437416.asp">Full Story</a>
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td valign="top" class="imagecredit8">AP Photo &#150; PETER DEJONG
		</td>
		<td valign="top" align="right" class="time8">&nbsp;
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td valign="top" colspan="3">&nbsp;
		</td>
	</tr>





	<tr>
		<td valign="top" class="headline8" colspan="2">Arabs Outside Iraq Stunned, Apprehensive About Collapse of Saddam's Regime in Baghdad</td>
		<td valign="top" rowspan="3" width="95" class="imagecredit8"><a href="/news/data/8_ds_437239.asp"><img src="/dsdsmultimedia/photos/TOPIX_EGYPT_IRAQ_WAR1.jpg" width="85" border="0"></a></td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td valign="top" colspan="2" class="citation8">Arabs responded Thursday to the sudden collapse of Saddam Hussein's government with anger, shock and even disbelief. One newspaper refused to acknowledge that Baghdad had fallen.&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="/news/data/8_ds_437239.asp">Full Story</a>
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td valign="top" class="imagecredit8">AP Photo &#150; AMR NABIL
		</td>
		<td valign="top" align="right" class="time8">&nbsp;
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td valign="top" colspan="3">&nbsp;
		</td>
	</tr>





	<tr>
		<td valign="top" class="headline8" colspan="2">Hong Kong Announces Quarantine of SARS Patients' Households</td>
		<td valign="top" rowspan="3" width="95" class="imagecredit8"><a href="/news/data/8_ds_437290.asp"><img src="/dsdsmultimedia/photos/HONG_KONG_SARS17.jpg" width="85" border="0"></a></td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td valign="top" colspan="2" class="citation8">Hong Kong said Thursday it will quarantine for up to 10 days anyone who resides with a confirmed SARS patient, in a tough measure to halt the spread of a disease that has killed 30 and sickened almost 1,000 in this city alone.&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="/news/data/8_ds_437290.asp">Full Story</a>
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td valign="top" class="imagecredit8">AP Photo &#150; ANAT GIVON
		</td>
		<td valign="top" align="right" class="time8">&nbsp;
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td valign="top" colspan="3">&nbsp;
		</td>
	</tr>





	<tr>
		<td valign="top" class="headline8" colspan="2">British, French Operators to End Concorde Service This Year Due to Slow Demand</td>
		<td valign="top" rowspan="3" width="95" class="imagecredit8"><a href="/news/data/8_ds_437487.asp"><img src="/dsdsmultimedia/photos/BRITAIN_CONCORDE.jpg" width="85" border="0"></a></td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td valign="top" colspan="2" class="citation8">Concorde, the chic needle-nosed jet that has flown stars and tycoons across the Atlantic at supersonic speeds and stratospheric cost for a quarter century, will be retired this year, its British and French operators said Thursday.&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="/news/data/8_ds_437487.asp">Full Story</a>
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td valign="top" class="imagecredit8">AP Photo &#150; 
		</td>
		<td valign="top" align="right" class="time8">&nbsp;
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td valign="top" colspan="3">&nbsp;
		</td>
	</tr>






	<tr>
		<td valign="top" class="headline8" colspan="3">News Corp. Reaches $6.6 Billion Deal Giving It Control of DirecTV Satellite Network</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td valign="top" colspan="3" class="citation8">News Corp. has reached a deal to gain control of Hughes Electronics Corp. and its DirecTV service, giving Australian media magnate Rupert Murdoch a U.S. outlet for his global satellite television network.&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="/news/data/8_ds_437234.asp">Full Story</a>
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td valign="top" colspan="3">&nbsp;
		</td>
	</tr>





	<tr>
		<td valign="top" class="headline8" colspan="3">Dow Likely to Rally After Fall of Kirkuk, Rising 20 Points to 8,200</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td valign="top" colspan="3" class="citation8">After trending lower for most of Thursday morning, the U.S. futures market rallied on news of the fall of Kirkuk in Iraq. Dow Jones futures were up 20 points to 8,200. Nasdaq futures increased 4.50 points, and S&amp;P futures rose by 1.50 points.&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="/news/data/8_ds_437736.asp">Full Story</a>
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td valign="top" colspan="3">&nbsp;
		</td>
	</tr>




	<tr>
		<td valign="top" class="headline8" colspan="2">Tiger Woods Seeks Third Straight Green Jacket As Members Make Defiant Stand to Kick Off Masters</td>
		<td valign="top" rowspan="3" width="95" class="imagecredit8"><a href="/news/data/8_ds_437797.asp"><img src="/dsdsmultimedia/photos/MASTERS186.jpg" width="85" border="0"></a></td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td valign="top" colspan="2" class="citation8">The men in green stood together, a defiant show of support for Augusta National Golf Club and its steadfast belief that only men should wear those coveted jackets.&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="/news/data/8_ds_437797.asp">Full Story</a>
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td valign="top" class="imagecredit8">AP Photo &#150; CHRIS O'MEARA
		</td>
		<td valign="top" align="right" class="time8">&nbsp;
		</td>
	</tr>
